        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "To be clear: LSP progress messages should be fine; the API for that is now official and documented. What's not fine is general notifications, since Neovim lacks the possibility of annotating messages so you have to rely on heuristics or extensive user configuration to decide what should be shown as a transient notification and what should be a persistent message. (Also vaguely planned, but not in the near future.)\r\n\r\nI personally would be interested in a progress notifier alone; but I'm not sure whether you wouldn't consider this too niche to warrant a mini.plugin.",
            "created_at": "2023-06-11T08:30:18Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/359#issuecomment-1586074182",
